 60GE c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster) October 5, 2005                        
 60GE c  {+60}Ge isotope produced in fragmentation of {+78}Kr{+34+} beam in a   
 60GE2c  {+9}Be target at E=140 MeV/nucleon.  Reaction products selected        
 60GE3c  according to their momentum/charge ratio using the A1900               
 60GE4c  spectrometer of the National Superconducting Cyclotron                 
 60GE5c  Laboratory (NSCL).                                                     
 60GE c  Measured fragments, tof and energy losses, timing scintillator (SCI),  
 60GE2c  a position-sensitive parallel-plate avalanche counter (PPAC) and three 
 60GE3c  silicon detectors (PIN). Half-life deduced from production yields      
 60GE c  Three events were assigned to {+60}Ge.                                 
